    {
      "claim_text": "VACUUM FULL is the faster of the two because it compacts the table in a single pass.",
      "verdict": "CONTRADICTED",
      "reasoning": "The passage states that VACUUM FULL runs much more slowly, not faster, and does not mention it compacts the table in a single pass.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "quote": "VACUUM FULL can reclaim more disk space but runs much more slowly."
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "quote": "VACUUM FULL actively compacts tables by writing a complete new version of the table file with no dead space. This minimizes the size of the table, but can take a long time."
